  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the calculation of an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (1225), then evaluating the probability of outcomes exceeding this level. Lottery B has a higher probability (34%) of exceeding the aspiration level compared to Lottery A (33%), so the reason would prefer B. The individual’s justification, however, is based on the perception that the outcomes are similar in value and thus choosing the lottery with the highest probability of any gain. This is not equivalent to evaluating positive differences relative to an aspiration level. While both the reason and the individual end up favoring Lottery B, the individual’s deliberation process does not involve the aspiration level or differences from it. The individual’s focus is on the probability of a non-zero outcome, not on a reference point derived from the mean of all outcomes. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the individual’s reasoning process.",
